WEBVTT

00:01.774 --> 00:04.842
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.910 --> 00:08.246
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.313 --> 00:11.382
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.450 --> 00:14.352
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.420 --> 00:18.289
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.373 --> 00:21.242
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.293 --> 00:22.827
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.895 --> 00:24.212
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.279 --> 00:26.981
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.608 --> 00:38.208
(Peter giggling)

00:43.314 --> 00:45.149
(Peter guffawing)

00:45.259 --> 00:46.794
LOIS:
Peter, what the hell
are you doing?

00:47.514 --> 00:48.514
I can't sleep, Lois.

00:48.602 --> 00:49.952
I'm too excited
for my birthday tomorrow.

00:50.019 --> 00:52.187
(giggling)
Yeah!

00:52.239 --> 00:53.973
Peter, would you get
in the damn bed?

00:54.040 --> 00:56.125
I'm gonna have
the best birthday party ever.

00:56.193 --> 00:58.194
I gave out
all my invitations yesterday.

00:58.261 --> 01:00.412
Hey, Chris, um,
I was wondering

01:00.480 --> 01:02.081
if you'd like to come
to my party tomorrow.

01:02.149 --> 01:04.016
Thanks, Dad.
I'd love to--

01:04.100 --> 01:05.985
Oh no! M-E-G.

01:06.069 --> 01:07.203
Hey.

01:07.270 --> 01:08.237
What are you guys
talking about?

01:08.305 --> 01:09.371
Uh, nothing.
Sports!

01:09.439 --> 01:10.840
Birthday sports!
No, just sports!

01:10.907 --> 01:12.007
Oh. Okay.

01:14.861 --> 01:16.929
Meg, you're not invited
to my party.

01:20.433 --> 01:23.335
Happy birthday,
sweetheart.

01:23.403 --> 01:25.871
Why don't you open your
presents while I cut the cake?

01:27.557 --> 01:29.441
Whoa!

01:29.509 --> 01:31.177
What planet is this?!

01:31.244 --> 01:32.695
It's not a pla--
Peter, it's Earth.

01:32.762 --> 01:33.913
It's a globe.

01:33.980 --> 01:35.881
You use it to learn
where the countries are.

01:35.949 --> 01:38.667
You gave me an educational toy?

01:38.735 --> 01:40.536
What do you say
to Mr. Swanson?

01:42.873 --> 01:44.890
(groans)
Thank you.

01:44.958 --> 01:48.177
Hey, Dad. This came
in the mail for you.

01:48.244 --> 01:49.511
A card?

01:49.579 --> 01:50.946
Oh, look, it's
one of those cards

01:51.014 --> 01:52.448
where you can record
your own message.

01:52.515 --> 01:54.149
Come on!
Open it up.

01:54.217 --> 01:55.551
CLEVELAND (on recording):
Hi, Peter!

01:55.619 --> 01:57.086
Happy birthday.

01:57.153 --> 01:59.421
Just wanted to send
our wishes from Virginia.

01:59.489 --> 02:00.656
Bye!

02:00.724 --> 02:02.258
Okay, Donna, I'm done.

02:02.325 --> 02:03.993
I'm gonna go mail this card.

02:04.060 --> 02:05.160
(door opens)

02:05.228 --> 02:06.996
(footfalls)

02:07.063 --> 02:08.998
(car door closes, engine starts)

02:09.065 --> 02:10.966
(radio turns on,
"Mmmbop" plays)

02:11.034 --> 02:13.135
CLEVELAND (singing along):
♪ Mmmbop, ba duba dop ba ♪

02:13.203 --> 02:16.272
♪ Boom bop, ba dubie dop
ba boom bop ♪

02:16.339 --> 02:18.641
♪ Dubie dop ba boom bop ♪

02:18.708 --> 02:20.175
♪ Oh yeah ♪

02:20.243 --> 02:23.045
♪ Mmmbop,
bi bada bop boom bop ♪

02:23.113 --> 02:24.146
(police siren wails)

02:24.214 --> 02:25.848
Oh, (bleep).

02:25.916 --> 02:28.217
Afternoon, Officer.

02:28.285 --> 02:30.052
OFFICER: Any idea
how fast you were goin'?

02:30.120 --> 02:31.353
CLEVELAND:
Uh, no, sir.

02:31.421 --> 02:32.821
OFFICER: You gettin' smart
with me, boy?

02:32.889 --> 02:33.989
Where'd you get them wheels?

02:34.057 --> 02:35.257
CLEVELAND:
Aw, come on, man.

02:35.325 --> 02:36.458
OFFICER:
Step out of the car.

02:36.526 --> 02:37.559
CLEVELAND:
But I ain't done nothin'.

02:37.627 --> 02:38.827
OFFICER:
Hands behind your back.

02:38.895 --> 02:40.195
CLEVELAND:
Hey, easy, watch it!

02:40.263 --> 02:41.397
OFFICER: Come on.
Don't you fight me, boy!

02:41.464 --> 02:42.531
Get down on the ground!

02:42.599 --> 02:43.432
CLEVELAND:
Come on! No!

02:43.500 --> 02:44.533
(running footsteps)

02:44.601 --> 02:45.467
OFFICER:
Hey! Get back here!

02:45.535 --> 02:46.568
(gunshot)

02:46.636 --> 02:47.803
CLEVELAND:
Aah! My arm!

02:47.871 --> 02:49.338
(running footsteps,
Cleveland panting)

02:52.409 --> 02:54.476
This looks like
a safe place to rest.

02:54.544 --> 02:55.678
(dogs barking)

02:55.745 --> 02:56.946
OFFICER: I think
he went this way!

02:57.013 --> 02:58.414
Peter, close
the card.

02:58.481 --> 02:59.748
Yeah, I'm sure
he's fine.

03:01.318 --> 03:03.152
(Cleveland screaming,
shots firing)

03:03.219 --> 03:04.787
Here, Peter, why don't
you open my gift?

03:04.854 --> 03:06.088
Ooh, Zales!

03:06.156 --> 03:07.556
Eh, it's just
the box, Peter.

03:07.624 --> 03:10.092
Tickets
to "Foxy Boxing"?

03:10.160 --> 03:11.377
Yeah, it's this
cool thing

03:11.444 --> 03:13.162
where girls in bikinis
box each other.

03:13.229 --> 03:14.730
We're all going
Saturday night!

03:18.001 --> 03:19.835
(bell clangs)

03:21.554 --> 03:23.155
Man, would you
look at that?

03:23.223 --> 03:24.790
Two smokin'
hot chicks

03:24.858 --> 03:26.725
repeatedly striking
each other.

03:26.793 --> 03:28.460
Yeah, it reminds me
of Thanksgiving.

03:28.528 --> 03:29.945
Why does it remind
you of Thanksgiving?

03:30.013 --> 03:31.847
'Cause this is where
I come for Thanksgiving.

03:31.915 --> 03:34.266
ANNOUNCER:
Ladies and gentlemen, may
I have your attention, please?

03:34.334 --> 03:35.734
We've reached that
part of the evening

03:35.802 --> 03:38.337
when our house champion
takes on all challengers.

03:38.405 --> 03:41.340
Any of you lovely ladies like
to try your hand in the ring?

03:41.408 --> 03:42.424
Hey, Lois,
what do you think?

03:42.492 --> 03:43.959
You want to fight
that lady's boobs?

03:44.027 --> 03:46.161
What? No. I'm not
fighting anyone.

03:46.229 --> 03:48.647
Oh. Well, good thing
I made this plaster mold

03:48.715 --> 03:50.032
of your hand
and forearm.

03:50.100 --> 03:51.300
Hey, buddy!
Over here!

03:51.368 --> 03:54.036
I see a woman's hand
and forearm at table eight!

03:54.104 --> 03:55.971
Damn it, Peter!

03:56.022 --> 03:57.690
Please, Lois! Come on,
you got to fight her!

03:57.757 --> 03:58.791
It's gonna be great!
Come on, Lois!

03:58.858 --> 03:59.775
Get in there,
take her down!

03:59.843 --> 04:00.859
Come on!
It'll be awesome!

04:00.944 --> 04:01.994
I'd really like
to see that.

04:02.078 --> 04:03.462
(sighs)
All right, all right.

04:03.530 --> 04:05.597
If it'll shut
you all up, I'll do it.

04:05.665 --> 04:07.166
(bell clangs)

04:09.586 --> 04:10.969
All right, so how
does this work?

04:11.037 --> 04:12.271
We gonna pretend
to hit each other

04:12.339 --> 04:14.340
for a while, then maybe
kiss a little? Huh?

04:14.407 --> 04:15.424
(laughing)

04:15.491 --> 04:17.059
I'm terrible.

04:17.127 --> 04:18.427
Hey, watch it.

04:18.495 --> 04:19.728
That was pretty hard.

04:19.796 --> 04:21.747
No, it wasn't.
Try this one.

04:21.831 --> 04:23.632
Stop that, young lady.

04:23.700 --> 04:25.751
I'm just out here for fun--

04:25.835 --> 04:27.836
PETER:
Yeah, punch each other,
you whores!

04:27.904 --> 04:30.572
Okay, you little bitch,
that's it!

04:30.640 --> 04:31.824
You want to (bleep) with me?!

04:31.891 --> 04:32.891
Let's go!

04:38.732 --> 04:41.667
No matter what you do
for the rest of your life,

04:41.735 --> 04:45.270
you'll always
be garbage.

04:45.355 --> 04:47.255
(crowd cheering)

04:47.307 --> 04:48.440
Oh, my God!

04:48.508 --> 04:50.592
I didn't know Lois
had that in her.

04:50.643 --> 04:51.810
Hey, is that
your wife?

04:51.878 --> 04:53.712
You bet that's my wife.

04:53.780 --> 04:55.547
Well, I got to say,
she's a natural.

04:55.615 --> 04:58.667
You know, she could make some
serious money as a professional.

04:58.735 --> 05:00.702
Wow, you-you
really think so?

05:00.770 --> 05:02.471
Oh, sure. Women's boxing

05:02.539 --> 05:04.323
is a rapidly growing
part of the field.

05:04.391 --> 05:06.992
You should consider your
wife competing for a belt.

05:07.060 --> 05:09.495
Well, she did look like she knew
what she was doin' up there.

05:09.562 --> 05:11.263
Think about it.
Here's my card.

05:14.150 --> 05:16.585
(chuckles)
What can I say?

05:16.636 --> 05:17.936
I really like
watching her box.

05:18.004 --> 05:19.405
That means
two things.

05:26.089 --> 05:27.046
Hey, Lois,
congrats

05:27.146 --> 05:28.997
on winning that
boxing match last night.

05:29.082 --> 05:30.632
<i>I saw your picture
in The Daily Growl.</i>

05:30.700 --> 05:33.135
<i>Brian, The Daily Growl
is not a real paper.</i>

05:33.203 --> 05:34.369
What? Yeah, it is.

05:34.437 --> 05:35.587
(squeaking)

05:35.655 --> 05:37.990
(laughing)
I like that sound.

05:38.057 --> 05:39.308
(squeaking)

05:39.375 --> 05:41.009
Mom, since when
are you a boxer?

05:41.077 --> 05:42.444
I'm not, honey.

05:42.512 --> 05:45.080
Honestly, I don't know what
came over me last night.

05:45.148 --> 05:47.082
It was just one
of those crazy things

05:47.150 --> 05:49.084
that sort of happened
after a few drinks.

05:49.152 --> 05:50.352
Morning, everyone!

05:50.420 --> 05:52.337
Morning, champ!
Ya feelin' loose today?

05:52.388 --> 05:53.672
Peter, what
are you doing?

05:53.740 --> 05:55.073
What is all this?

05:55.141 --> 05:56.341
I'm a fight promoter now.

05:56.409 --> 05:57.876
And I got you another fight.

05:57.944 --> 06:00.095
You're boxing tonight
at the Quahog Civic Center.

06:00.163 --> 06:01.496
Are you out
of your mind?

06:01.564 --> 06:04.499
No, Peter. That was a
one-time thing, all right?

06:04.567 --> 06:06.802
I am not a boxer, and I'm
not fighting anyone else.

06:06.870 --> 06:08.003
And that's final.

06:08.071 --> 06:09.438
All right, well,
how about this, then?

06:09.505 --> 06:12.241
I'll take you somewhere real
fancy and romantic for dinner,

06:12.308 --> 06:13.609
just the two of us.

06:13.676 --> 06:15.777
And in return, I get to try
and convince you to fight.

06:15.845 --> 06:18.013
Well, going out for
dinner would be nice.

06:18.081 --> 06:20.332
But I'm not
changing my mind.

06:20.383 --> 06:23.335
Oh, gosh, I can't wait to
see this fancy restaurant.

06:23.403 --> 06:25.320
Oh, you're gonna
love it, Lois.

06:25.388 --> 06:28.090
Here, put on these special
eating gloves I bought you.

06:28.157 --> 06:30.759
Why do I need to wear gloves
to eat in a fancy restaurant?

06:30.827 --> 06:32.961
'Cause it's
so fancy that-that...

06:33.029 --> 06:34.513
You know what?
I'm tired of this.

06:34.564 --> 06:35.714
I booked you
a boxing match.

06:35.765 --> 06:37.232
Son of a bitch!

06:37.317 --> 06:40.102
Damn it, Peter. I told you,
I don't want to be a boxer!

06:40.169 --> 06:42.004
Who the hell do you
think you are?!

06:42.071 --> 06:43.605
There you go!
Use that anger!

06:43.673 --> 06:45.107
Hey, remember when
I said I think it's hot

06:45.174 --> 06:46.642
when you wear a sports bra
and gym shorts

06:46.709 --> 06:47.809
underneath your dress?

06:47.877 --> 06:48.911
Yeah?

06:48.995 --> 06:50.028
Now, put
these shoes on.

06:50.079 --> 06:51.280
Stop it,
you jackass!

06:51.347 --> 06:54.666
I told you, I'm
not fighting!

06:54.734 --> 06:57.336
I'm sorry, there's been
a terrible mistake.

06:57.403 --> 06:58.670
My idiot husband here
booked this match

06:58.738 --> 06:59.838
without my knowledge--

06:59.906 --> 07:01.273
(bell clangs)

07:01.341 --> 07:02.357
PETER:
She's from the
Ukraine, Lois!

07:02.425 --> 07:03.558
She doesn't speak English!

07:03.626 --> 07:04.927
All right.

07:04.994 --> 07:07.062
(Lois speaking in
Ukranian dialect)

07:07.146 --> 07:08.730
PETER:
She's from the other
part of the Ukraine!

07:08.798 --> 07:10.632
It's a different dialect!

07:12.852 --> 07:15.320
One, two, three.

07:19.008 --> 07:21.109
Hey! Whatcha doin'
down there, Lois?

07:22.478 --> 07:23.812
Aw, what's the matter?

07:23.880 --> 07:26.048
Mad at little old me?

07:26.115 --> 07:28.884
In your imagination,
I've got long eyelashes.

07:28.952 --> 07:31.453
(growling)

07:43.616 --> 07:45.217
(panting)

07:45.284 --> 07:47.753
One! Two! Three!

07:47.820 --> 07:49.954
Did you know where the Ukraine
was 'cause of my globe?

07:50.006 --> 07:51.456
No, I saw it in a book.

07:51.524 --> 07:54.443
You knew 'cause
of my globe, you dick.

07:54.510 --> 07:56.745
Eight! Nine! Ten!

07:56.813 --> 07:58.230
We have a winner!

07:58.297 --> 07:59.915
(crowd cheering)

07:59.999 --> 08:01.533
Well, what do you
think of that, Lois?

08:01.584 --> 08:02.784
You still mad at me now?

08:02.869 --> 08:04.619
Peter!
I feel great!

08:04.704 --> 08:06.755
I've never felt
so in control.

08:06.839 --> 08:08.256
I know the feeling.

08:08.341 --> 08:10.342
It's how I feel when
I burp really loud

08:10.409 --> 08:11.743
in an underground
parking structure

08:11.794 --> 08:13.311
to assert my dominance.

08:13.379 --> 08:15.814
(belches, belch echoes)

08:15.882 --> 08:17.849
Says the king.

08:21.020 --> 08:23.555
All right, kids, I'm off
to train at the gym.

08:23.623 --> 08:26.258
Geez, Lois, you're really
taking this seriously, huh?

08:26.325 --> 08:28.093
Well, yeah, Brian,
why wouldn't I?

08:28.161 --> 08:29.661
I don't know,
you've just never

08:29.729 --> 08:31.063
really been
the aggressive type.

08:31.130 --> 08:34.032
I mean, you're usually
so measured and collected.

08:34.100 --> 08:37.069
I know, Brian, but when
I stepped into that ring--

08:37.136 --> 08:39.671
I don't know.
Something happened to me.

08:39.739 --> 08:42.407
It's like I tapped
into this primal wellspring

08:42.475 --> 08:45.243
of pent-up anger that
just needed to be released.

08:45.311 --> 08:47.345
Really? What do you
have to be angry about?

08:47.413 --> 08:51.016
Where are my flapjacks?!

08:51.084 --> 08:51.883
Huh?

08:51.951 --> 08:53.518
You will recall, last night,

08:53.586 --> 08:55.587
ere I drifted off into slumber

08:55.655 --> 08:57.756
with a nudie magazine
betwixt my legs,

08:57.824 --> 08:59.191
I spake thusly:

08:59.258 --> 09:01.693
"Lois, tomorrow morning,
I want flapjacks."

09:01.761 --> 09:04.996
It was a simple message,
yet it has gone unheeded.

09:05.064 --> 09:06.631
(low growl)

09:06.699 --> 09:08.467
All right, Peter,
give me a minute.

09:08.534 --> 09:10.936
For every five seconds
I do not have flapjacks,

09:11.003 --> 09:13.588
I shall break one window.

09:13.673 --> 09:15.407
Uh-huh.

09:15.475 --> 09:16.842
Look, Lois,
it just seems to me

09:16.909 --> 09:18.677
that this isn't necessarily
the healthiest thing

09:18.745 --> 09:20.278
for a woman your age
to be doing.

09:20.346 --> 09:21.747
(glass breaking)

09:21.814 --> 09:23.682
Brian, I'm 42, I'm in
the prime of my life,

09:23.750 --> 09:25.250
and this is what
I want right now.

09:25.318 --> 09:26.384
You're sure
about that?

09:26.452 --> 09:27.652
(glass breaking)

09:27.720 --> 09:29.421
Meg, go make your
father some flapjacks.

09:29.489 --> 09:31.056
(sighs)
Okay, Mom.

09:31.124 --> 09:32.107
(glass breaking)

09:32.175 --> 09:33.375
PETER:
This is crazy!

09:33.443 --> 09:35.177
Is nobody really
making me flapjacks yet?

09:35.244 --> 09:38.513
At this point, you guys are
being as irresponsible as I am!

09:38.581 --> 09:41.083
("Gonna Fly Now" playing)

09:41.167 --> 09:43.835
♪ ♪

09:53.379 --> 09:58.683
♪ Gonna fly now ♪

09:58.751 --> 10:03.822
♪ Flying high now ♪

10:03.890 --> 10:08.927
♪ Gonna fly ♪

10:08.995 --> 10:13.732
♪ Fly... fly! ♪

10:13.800 --> 10:14.966
(punch cracks)

10:20.173 --> 10:22.140
(gasps)
Ow!

10:22.208 --> 10:23.408
Well, it's broken,
all right.

10:23.476 --> 10:24.659
Well, you got
to fix her, Doc.

10:24.744 --> 10:25.844
There's a big fight
coming up.

10:25.912 --> 10:26.912
She's got to
defend her title.

10:26.979 --> 10:28.280
Look, Peter,
I don't think

10:28.347 --> 10:29.414
there's gonna
be any fight.

10:29.482 --> 10:30.515
What are you
talking about?

10:30.583 --> 10:32.818
Look at me.
I got a broken nose.

10:32.885 --> 10:35.053
I think this is a sign
that maybe it's time

10:35.121 --> 10:36.254
to hang up the gloves.

10:36.322 --> 10:37.839
What are you,
out of your mind?

10:37.907 --> 10:39.674
Whoa, don't you give me
that attitude, Peter.

10:39.742 --> 10:42.310
Look, Lois, we're making a lot
of cash with this boxing thing.

10:42.378 --> 10:44.713
And I need money
for bourbon and anime.

10:44.780 --> 10:46.982
(slurring):
Well, I just can't understand
any of this.

10:47.049 --> 10:48.650
Everybody in Japan

10:48.718 --> 10:51.553
is either a ten-year-old girl
or a monster.

10:51.621 --> 10:53.355
I don't care about
the money, Peter!

10:53.422 --> 10:54.656
I don't care
about boxing!

10:54.724 --> 10:56.791
The only reason I did
this in the first place

10:56.859 --> 10:58.627
was 'cause of you!
What do you mean?

10:58.694 --> 11:00.829
Peter, sometimes
you're so insensitive,

11:00.897 --> 11:03.965
and you make me so angry, I just
want to clock you in the jaw.

11:04.033 --> 11:05.817
Obviously, I
can't do that,

11:05.885 --> 11:07.285
so boxing was
an outlet.

11:07.353 --> 11:11.056
Wait, you mean the reason
you fight so good is...

11:11.123 --> 11:13.508
Yeah, 'cause I'm making
believe I'm fighting you!

11:13.576 --> 11:17.012
Wow. Am I that
much of a bastard?

11:17.079 --> 11:18.446
Sometimes, yes.

11:18.514 --> 11:20.515
Geez, Lois, I'm sorry.

11:20.583 --> 11:22.784
I-I... I mean,
I don't mean to be,

11:22.852 --> 11:24.186
I just...

11:24.253 --> 11:26.788
Look, if you don't want
to fight anymore,

11:26.856 --> 11:28.290
you don't have to.

11:28.357 --> 11:29.558
Well, good.

11:29.625 --> 11:32.227
A-And the truth is,
I suppose I kind of got

11:32.295 --> 11:34.129
most of it out of
my system anyway.

11:34.197 --> 11:36.131
Oh, I love you, Lois.

11:36.199 --> 11:38.266
I love you, too, Peter.

11:38.334 --> 11:40.318
Is it cool if I tell
your insurance

11:40.386 --> 11:41.786
that I gave you
heart surgery?

11:45.157 --> 11:48.109
Ladies and gentlemen,
in honor of her retirement

11:48.177 --> 11:51.329
after 17 consecutive
victories,

11:51.397 --> 11:55.700
I hereby dedicate this statue
to Quahog's greatest fighter,

11:55.768 --> 11:57.586
Lois Griffin!

11:59.355 --> 12:01.339
(whistling, whooping)

12:01.390 --> 12:03.725
I'm also having
a celebratory keg party

12:03.793 --> 12:05.527
back at my house later.

12:05.595 --> 12:09.297
You can tell your parents
that my parents will be there.

12:09.365 --> 12:11.233
(chuckles)
But they won't be.

12:11.317 --> 12:13.184
(cheering)

12:13.236 --> 12:16.404
And now a few words
from Lois Griffin herself.

12:17.823 --> 12:19.658
Thank you so much
for coming, everyone,

12:19.725 --> 12:23.144
and thank you for always
cheering me on at all my fights.

12:23.212 --> 12:24.179
WOMAN:
Hey, Griffin!

12:26.449 --> 12:29.017
Oh, my God, that's Deirdre Jackson!
Who's that?

12:29.085 --> 12:31.870
Only the deadliest fighter
in all of women's boxing.

12:31.938 --> 12:34.072
She's killed three
people in the ring.

12:34.140 --> 12:35.957
BRIAN:
Her fists are so dangerous,

12:36.042 --> 12:38.093
<i>she's not allowed
to be a lesbian.</i>

12:38.177 --> 12:39.527
I know why you're
retiring, Griffin!

12:39.595 --> 12:40.562
You're scared!

12:40.630 --> 12:42.530
Scared? Of what?

12:42.598 --> 12:44.883
Of me! Look at these people,
giving you a statue

12:44.951 --> 12:46.451
for fighting a bunch of bums!

12:46.519 --> 12:49.271
If you're so great, why don't
you prove it? Fight me!

12:49.338 --> 12:51.473
Look, I don't need
to prove anything.

12:51.540 --> 12:54.342
I'm retired, and that's
the way it's gonna stay.

12:54.410 --> 12:55.610
Oh, yeah?

12:55.678 --> 12:57.145
<i>Hey, man, you want
a real woman?</i>

12:57.213 --> 12:58.980
Why don't you bring
your pretty little self

12:59.048 --> 13:00.231
over to my
apartment tonight,

13:00.299 --> 13:01.533
<i>and I'll show you
a real woman.</i>

13:01.600 --> 13:03.435
Oh, I'm ashamed!

13:03.502 --> 13:05.303
Hey, that's my husband
you're talking to!

13:05.371 --> 13:07.489
Yeah? Well, what are
you gonna do about it?

13:07.556 --> 13:08.623
You gonna fight me?

13:08.691 --> 13:09.824
Look, I already said...

13:09.892 --> 13:11.459
Get down on your
hands and knees, fatty!

13:11.527 --> 13:12.394
Yeah! Yes, sir!

13:14.997 --> 13:17.332
Look at me, Griffin--
I'm milking me a cow!

13:17.416 --> 13:18.667
Moo for me!

13:18.751 --> 13:19.801
Moo.
Louder!

13:19.885 --> 13:21.052
Moo!
Louder!

13:21.120 --> 13:22.637
Moo...!
Louder!

13:22.705 --> 13:24.139
(sobbing):
Moo...!

13:24.206 --> 13:25.390
All right, that's it!

13:25.457 --> 13:27.175
You want a fight,
you got one!

13:27.243 --> 13:29.210
Now, you get your
hands off my man

13:29.278 --> 13:31.012
before I break 'em off!

13:32.748 --> 13:34.249
(bleep)!
It's my parents!

13:34.317 --> 13:35.717
The party's off, everybody!

13:35.785 --> 13:37.185
Get the (bleep) out of here!

13:43.953 --> 13:45.303
Good evening.
I'm Tom Tucker.

13:45.371 --> 13:47.205
Coming up next, a boxing match

13:47.256 --> 13:49.707
<i>where the fighters are bleeding
before the fight?</i>

13:49.759 --> 13:52.444
We've got exclusive coverage of
tonight's women's boxing bout,

13:52.512 --> 13:54.279
Griffin versus Jackson.

13:54.347 --> 13:57.549
We're here live with contender Deirdre
Jackson outside her dressing room.

13:57.600 --> 14:00.769
Deirdre, is it true you've
killed three women in the ring?

14:00.837 --> 14:02.387
Tonight it's
gonna be four.

14:02.455 --> 14:05.107
Are you saying you intend
to kill your opponent?

14:05.191 --> 14:08.643
Let's just say you
don't want to miss round six.

14:08.711 --> 14:10.929
(gasps)
Lois, you can't go out tre!

14:10.997 --> 14:13.598
What? Why not?
Because if you step into that ring,

14:13.666 --> 14:14.866
she's gonna kill you.

14:14.934 --> 14:16.101
No, she's not, Peter.

14:16.169 --> 14:18.170
What the hell kind
of talk is that?

14:18.237 --> 14:19.654
Now, I'm gonna
win this thing.

14:19.722 --> 14:21.857
Look, Lois, you don't
have to do this for me.

14:21.924 --> 14:23.358
I know I make you
mad sometimes,

14:23.426 --> 14:25.694
but I thought we agreed
you'd hang up the gloves.

14:25.762 --> 14:28.630
I'll hang up the gloves
after I knock her ass out.

14:28.698 --> 14:29.931
Peter, she milked
your boobs,

14:29.999 --> 14:32.501
and there were a lot of
people I knew there.

14:32.568 --> 14:33.769
Now, let's go.

14:35.688 --> 14:37.255
MAN:
Butt scratcher!

14:37.323 --> 14:39.591
Get your butt scratcher here!

14:39.659 --> 14:41.460
Now, since this is
a televised boxing match,

14:41.527 --> 14:42.627
I'm gonna be joined

14:42.695 --> 14:44.429
by a horribly disfigured
former fighter

14:44.497 --> 14:46.731
providing barely intelligible
commentary throughout.

14:46.799 --> 14:48.600
Any thoughts on
the fight, Floyd?

14:48.651 --> 14:50.619
Uh, I-I think that they're...
they're gonna have,

14:50.686 --> 14:52.754
they are gonna be fightin'
Deirdre's last fight

14:52.822 --> 14:54.639
in the contrast
to the later one

14:54.707 --> 14:56.441
is gonna be bet-better
than usually.

14:56.509 --> 14:59.110
And how do you think that
helps her chances tonight?

14:59.178 --> 15:02.981
Well, the match lastin' the bout up
until the particular inaccuracy,

15:03.049 --> 15:06.785
particular unusually that should
be the ultimate determining factor

15:06.853 --> 15:08.320
in about the
12-round experience,

15:08.387 --> 15:10.155
the heart of a champion
margarine hat.

15:10.223 --> 15:11.857
Well, we'll be
watching for that.

15:11.924 --> 15:14.092
We'll be checking in with you
throughout the night, Floyd.

15:14.160 --> 15:15.594
And happy 23rd birthday.

15:15.661 --> 15:16.728
You're welcome.

15:18.548 --> 15:22.133
Ladies and gentlemen, may
I have your attention, please?

15:22.201 --> 15:24.436
Introducing tonight's fighters.

15:24.504 --> 15:28.406
In this corner,
weighing in at 134 pounds,

15:28.474 --> 15:31.159
the top-ranked boxer
in all of Rhode Island,

15:31.244 --> 15:34.496
Deirdre "Action" Jackson!

15:34.580 --> 15:37.766
(crowd jeering)

15:39.435 --> 15:42.537
I think every Italian
in Quahog is here.

15:42.605 --> 15:44.372
Yeah! Go, white girl!

15:44.457 --> 15:47.275
Hey, yo, you're gettin'
your grinder on my grinder!

15:47.343 --> 15:51.446
And in this corner,
weighing in at 130 pounds,

15:51.514 --> 15:53.448
it's the Ovarian Barbarian

15:53.516 --> 15:56.017
and the Breast of All Time,

15:56.085 --> 15:58.904
let's put our hands together
for Quahog's own...

15:58.971 --> 16:00.856
Lois Griffin!

16:00.940 --> 16:03.225
(crowd cheering,
whistling, whooping)

16:03.309 --> 16:05.510
Okay, here's the rules.

16:05.578 --> 16:07.712
No hitting below the belt,

16:07.780 --> 16:10.549
no rabbit punches,
no name calling,

16:10.616 --> 16:12.384
no making trouble
for unconventional couples

16:12.451 --> 16:15.120
who want to adopt babies,
'cause you know what,

16:15.187 --> 16:17.055
they ain't gettin'
the good babies, anyways.

16:17.123 --> 16:18.857
Okay, have a fun fight.

16:18.925 --> 16:20.425
Ding, ding.

16:20.493 --> 16:21.459
(bell clangs)

16:24.447 --> 16:25.780
You think you're tough?

16:25.848 --> 16:27.582
Well, let's see what you got!

16:29.285 --> 16:30.719
(punches cracking)

16:30.803 --> 16:31.887
(punches smacking)

16:31.971 --> 16:34.005
(punches cracking)

16:37.510 --> 16:40.312
(punches cracking, thudding)

16:52.942 --> 16:55.210
Wow, she's really
hitting Mom hard.

16:55.278 --> 16:56.378
Good.

16:58.281 --> 16:59.564
(bell clangs)

16:59.615 --> 17:00.966
(panting)

17:05.121 --> 17:06.988
How you feeling, Lois?

17:07.056 --> 17:09.524
(gasping):
She... she's too str...

17:09.592 --> 17:11.376
she's too strong, Joe.

17:11.444 --> 17:13.595
I don't stand a
chance out there.

17:13.679 --> 17:15.947
All right, Lois, you listen
to me and you listen good.

17:16.015 --> 17:17.415
I held your hand
during childbirth,

17:17.483 --> 17:19.985
I watched you raise three kids
on a shoestring budget--

17:20.052 --> 17:22.687
you never gave up then,
and you're not giving up now!

17:22.755 --> 17:24.556
'Cause you're the toughest woman
I've ever met.

17:24.624 --> 17:26.791
And if there was
a hall of fame for hearts,

17:26.859 --> 17:29.561
yours would be the biggest one
in the whole damn building!

17:29.629 --> 17:31.363
QUAGMIRE:
Peter, you're in
the wrong corner!

17:31.430 --> 17:32.731
PETER:
Ah.

17:32.782 --> 17:34.883
All right, Lois, you listen
to me and you listen good.

17:34.951 --> 17:36.284
(bell clangs)
Damn it!

17:37.586 --> 17:39.120
(crowd jeering)

17:39.188 --> 17:41.122
Shut up!

17:41.190 --> 17:42.857
Everybody shut up!

17:42.925 --> 17:44.960
This took a lot of courage!

17:45.027 --> 17:47.562
Well, ladies and gentlemen,
here we are at round six--

17:47.630 --> 17:50.031
the round that Deirdre Jackson
predicted she'd kill Lois Griffin.

17:50.099 --> 17:53.001
What do you think, Floyd, is she
gonna make good on that promise?

17:53.069 --> 17:56.404
A broken promise is a lot
like a child's pinwheel.

17:56.472 --> 18:00.041
You have to b-be yourself,
or at least within the confines.

18:02.611 --> 18:05.246
All right, well, let's see
what's going on in the ring.

18:05.314 --> 18:06.548
(bell clangs)

18:08.317 --> 18:09.951
Finish this.

18:22.581 --> 18:25.149
(slow-motion, vicious grunt)

18:27.203 --> 18:30.038
(crowd ooh-ing)

18:37.713 --> 18:39.297
One, two...

18:40.916 --> 18:42.484
Lois, stay down.
Don't get up.

18:42.551 --> 18:43.885
You've got nothing to prove.

18:43.953 --> 18:46.104
...five, six...

18:46.172 --> 18:48.239
You get up, you die!

18:48.307 --> 18:49.708
(fierce grunt)

18:49.775 --> 18:51.793
I've had enough of you!

18:51.861 --> 18:53.845
("Eye of the Tiger" playing)

18:53.896 --> 18:56.731
(punches cracking, thudding)

19:03.039 --> 19:05.924
("Eye of the Tiger" continues)

19:13.149 --> 19:16.451
♪ ♪

19:28.597 --> 19:30.515
♪ ♪

19:30.583 --> 19:32.317
♪ Risin' up ♪

19:32.384 --> 19:35.019
♪ Back on the street ♪

19:35.087 --> 19:37.422
♪ Did my time,
took my chances... ♪

19:37.490 --> 19:39.390
Oh, get out of here.
Yeah, okay.

19:39.458 --> 19:41.159
(punches cracking)

19:52.404 --> 19:53.805
You're goin'
down, Griffin!

19:55.574 --> 19:57.559
Not tonight, I'm not!

19:57.626 --> 19:58.877
(grunts)

20:00.930 --> 20:02.781
(slow-motion thud)

20:12.825 --> 20:14.776
(cheering, whistling)

20:19.698 --> 20:21.399
Lois! You did it!

20:21.467 --> 20:23.318
I love you so much!

20:23.402 --> 20:25.053
And the
winner is...

20:25.121 --> 20:27.539
Lois Griffin!

20:27.606 --> 20:30.274
Now, if everyone could just pick
up two chairs before you leave,

20:30.326 --> 20:32.460
we can get this place
cleaned up a lot quicker.

20:32.528 --> 20:34.295
Wow. Well, what do
you think, Floyd?

20:34.380 --> 20:36.981
How did Lois Griffin do what
no other challenger could do

20:37.049 --> 20:38.550
and knock out
Deirdre Jackson?

20:38.617 --> 20:41.769
I-I have a strong headache when
I go to sleep and wake up.

20:41.837 --> 20:44.556
And how do you think that's going
to affect Jackson's next fight?

20:44.623 --> 20:47.008
My Puerto Rican
wife got fat.

20:52.898 --> 20:55.183
Well, I gotta be honest,
Lois, I had my doubts,

20:55.251 --> 20:57.318
but you really held
your own in that ring.

20:57.386 --> 21:00.188
Thanks, Brian.
It was nice to go out a champion.

21:00.256 --> 21:01.890
Well, we're real proud
of you, Lois.

21:01.957 --> 21:04.792
And thanks to Deirdre,
I even got some of my own milk

21:04.860 --> 21:07.745
to put on my cereal.

21:07.813 --> 21:09.898
OTHERS:
Dad, come on! Oh, Peter!
Oh, for crying out loud!

21:09.965 --> 21:10.431
What? I'm fun.

21:10.432 --> 22:11.432
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru